**Halloway Park**
- Zone: spans the boundary between Residential Infill and The Hills, with its Gate sub-zone touching Downtown/Commercial Spine
- Type: major anchor park — the district's primary green space, modeled directly on Prospect Park's real internal structure
- Physical description: five distinct sub-zones under one park — The Wide Green (sweeping open meadow), The Hollow (wooded ravine terrain, the district's only true forest cover, and home to The Founders' Grove — real memorial markers for each of the twelve founding mothers, dedicated while living wherever possible, curated by Odessa Calloway's Keeping House), The Gate (where Greenleaf Stage sits, the threshold into Downtown's grid), scattered Pocket nodes (neighborhood playgrounds near Hearthstone), and The Quiet Water (a secluded riverside trail along Premium Riverfront's northern edge)
- History: named for Ruth Halloway; the park's trail network is the physical origin of the district's whole womb-node urban design philosophy (see St_Claire_00_Concept.md, Womb-Based Street & Trail Network)
- Units: not applicable — public park land, no tenant units

**Odessa Calloway's Keeping House**
- Zone: Historic Brick Core, Working Riverfront (Old Town) zone
- Type: converted rowhouse — community archive, functioning as a real lived-in home
- Physical description: three stories, rooms overflowing with community papers, oral history recordings, and donated personal collections — deliberately domestic rather than institutional, someone actually lives here full-time
- History: founded by Odessa Calloway, Founding Mother of history & oral tradition; the physical reason the parish's legacy survived its early-2000s closure
- Units: one — occupied by Odessa Calloway's Keeping House (cross-reference: St_Claire_05_Organizations.md)

**The Back Porch (storefront)**
- Zone: Historic Brick Core, Working Riverfront (Old Town) zone
- Type: commercial storefront with backyard
- Physical description: modest bar interior, but the real social space is the backyard — string lights, mismatched furniture, decades unchanged
- History: not yet determined
- Units: one — occupied by The Back Porch (cross-reference: St_Claire_05_Organizations.md)

