**St. Claire Reclamation Works (central processing facility)**
- Zone: Transition Zone — real open land, consistent with the zone's utilitarian character
- Type: waste-to-energy and water reclamation facility
- Physical description: a large industrial complex, genuinely functional rather than scenic — furnaces, boilers, water treatment tanks, and the biosolids drying operation all under one roof, with the underground hub network radiating outward from here district-wide
- History: built by Dr. Harriet Osei following the 1988 land-trust win
- Units: one — occupied by Harriet Osei – St. Claire Reclamation Works (cross-reference: St_Claire_05_Organizations.md)

**The Reclamation Hub Network (underground)**
- Zone: district-wide — reaches every zone via the underground utility web (see St_Claire_00_Concept.md, Collective Utility System)
- Type: underground infrastructure — waste collection hubs, steam and water distribution lines
- Physical description: entirely underground, invisible from street level; waste collection intake points throughout the district feed to intermediate hubs, which feed to the central processing facility
- History: built alongside the central facility, expanded incrementally as the district grew
- Units: not applicable — infrastructure, not tenant space

